# Defect 453, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's R3): `num`'s header
# makes `onefile_num` an `int` read alone, and a `long long` read after the
# other module's header, so `onefile_size` returns 4 in `build` and 8 in the
# one file `--emit-c` writes.
#
# Its modules are named for the key the compiler walks `use` lines by (panel
# 238's R4, `selfhost/use_key.hero`): `defines_wide` before `num`, so the one
# file reads the header that defines the macro first, the order the refusal
# is about. Read the other way the one file means what the units mean, and
# `--emit-c` writes it, correctly.
use defines_wide
use num

function main()
    print(num.size())
    print(defines_wide.bits())
